HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupGameHelp.0", "A single player game playing out a single map.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupGameHelp.1", "A single player game playing through a series of maps.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupGameHelp.2", "A multi-player game, with several human players competing against each other on a single map.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupGameHelp.3", "Cancel back to the main menu.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupMultiPlayerGameHelp.0", "Play a Hot Seat game, where 2 to 4 players play around the same computer, switching into the 'Hot Seat' when it is their turn.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupMultiPlayerGameHelp.1", "Play a network game, where 2 players use their own computers connected through a LAN (Local Area Network).")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupMultiPlayerGameHelp.2", "Play a modem game, where 2 players use ther own computers connected over the phone lines using modems.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupMultiPlayerGameHelp.3", "Play a direct connect game, where 2 players use ther own computers directly connected through their serial port by a null modem.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gSetupMultiPlayerGameHelp.4", "Cancel back to the main menu.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.0", "Accept these settings and start a new game.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.1", "Return to the main menu.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.2", "Challenge all computer players as 'King of the Hill'.  Computer players will be offended by your boastfulness, and lay off each other in an attempt to beat you to a pulp.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.3", "Select which scenario to play.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.4", "Change the starting difficulty at which you will play.  Higher difficulty levels start you off with fewer resources.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.5", "Change the difficulty of this opponent.  Smarter computer players are more aggressive and think longer for each turn.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.6", "Change your banner color.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.7", "The difficulty rating reflects a combination of various settings for your game.  This number will be applied to your final score.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gNewGameHelp.8", "Change the starting difficulty of another human player.  Higher difficulty levels start you off with fewer resources.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gLuckInfoText.0", "Good Luck\n\nGood luck sometimes lets your armies get lucky attacks (double strength) in combat.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gLuckInfoText.1", "Neutral Luck\n\nNeutral luck means your armies will never get lucky or unlucky attacks on the enemy.")
HOMM1_MESSAGE("table.gLuckInfoText.2", "Bad Luck\n\nBad luck sometimes falls on your armies in combat, causing their attacks to only do half damage.")
